From: rhodep port <none@example.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:35:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: ipa: an INIT_COMPLETED response means the uC is loaded

ipa_uc_response_hdlr() only sets uc_loaded when it also owns a power
reference for the microcontroller. If the response arrives without one it
warns and leaves the flag alone, which reads as bookkeeping and is not.

ipa_qmi_init_driver() builds its request with

	req.skip_uc_load = ipa->uc_loaded ? 1 : 0;

so a false flag asks the modem to load the microcontroller. Bind IPA while
the modem is already up -- as happens whenever the module is loaded by
hand, and after any modem restart, since ipa_uc_power() guards its body
with a file-scope static and runs once per module load -- and the uC has
been running since long before this driver existed. It answers, nobody
holds a reference, the flag stays false, and the AP then tells the modem
to load a microcontroller that is already running.

Observed on a Motorola rhodep. With the tracing patch on the QMI
handshake:

  ipa 5840000.ipa: unexpected init_completed response
  ipa-qmi: -> INIT_DRIVER hdr=[0x688..0x8c7] v4rt=0x508 v6rt=0x608
           v4flt=0x308 v6flt=0x408 modem=[0x27d8 +0x800] ctrl_ep=16
           skip_uc=0

Every address in that request is correct for this SoC; skip_uc is the one
thing wrong with it.

Set the flag from the response, which is what the response means, and
keep the power handling conditional on actually holding the reference.
The remaining warning is reworded to say what it now describes.

Signed-off-by: rhodep port <none@example.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ipa/ipa_uc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ipa/ipa_uc.c
@@ -155,13 +155,25 @@
 	 */
 	switch (shared->response) {
 	case IPA_UC_RESPONSE_INIT_COMPLETED:
+		/*
+		 * The microcontroller is telling us it finished initialising,
+		 * so it is loaded. That is true whether or not this driver is
+		 * the one that powered it: when IPA is bound with the modem
+		 * already running, the uC came up long ago and reports here
+		 * without uc_powered ever having been set.
+		 *
+		 * The flag matters beyond bookkeeping. ipa_qmi_init_driver()
+		 * sends skip_uc_load = uc_loaded, so leaving it false asks the
+		 * modem to load a microcontroller that is already running.
+		 */
+		ipa->uc_loaded = true;
+
 		if (ipa->uc_powered) {
-			ipa->uc_loaded = true;
 			ipa_power_retention(ipa, true);
 			(void)pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(dev);
 			ipa->uc_powered = false;
 		} else {
-			dev_warn(dev, "unexpected init_completed response\n");
+			dev_warn(dev, "init_completed with no power reference held\n");
 		}
 		break;
 	default:
